                    "group": "mysql",
                    "kind": "DataQuery",
                    "spec": {
                      "editorMode": "code",
                      "format": "table",
                      "rawQuery": true,
                      "rawSql": "-- Null baseline 65.8%: what randomly shuffled calls score at 30d under\n-- this grading scheme (scripts/check_null_baseline.py, seed 20260819,\n-- session 31). Re-derive whenever the bands or the action mix change --\n-- a stale null silently turns this tile back into a hit rate.\nSELECT ROUND(100*SUM(verdict='CORRECT')/\n  NULLIF(SUM(verdict IN('CORRECT','INCORRECT')),0) - 65.8, 1) AS v\nFROM recommendation_outcomes\nWHERE horizon_days=30 AND $__timeFilter(generated_at)"
                    },
                    "version": "v0"
                  },
                  "refId": "A"
                }
              }
            ],
            "queryOptions": {},
            "transformations": []
          }
        },
        "description": "The headline. Hit rate MINUS the rate skill-free calls score under this grading scheme (null = 65.8% at 30d), in percentage points. Positive means the calls beat chance; 0 means the scorecard is measuring the grading scheme rather than the system. The raw rate is the tile to the right \u2014 it is not interpretable on its own, because HOLD scores by standing still and WATCH by anything moving, and those two are 89% of all calls. Null pinned by scripts/check_null_baseline.py (session 31).",
        "id": 1,
        "links": [],
        "title": "Hit rate vs null (30d)",
